# Goal

Fix the HOD Dashboard so that it does not show the "New Application" option to HODs. Provide the HOD with only the necessary rights: to Approve, Reject, and Download the applicant's documents.

## Proposed Changes

### Frontend - HOD Dashboard Adjustments

#### [MODIFY] [layout.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/BHU%20INTERNSHIP%20PROJECT/frontend/src/app/dashboard/layout.tsx)
- Ensure the "New Application" button in the top navigation is strictly isolated to the Applicant role and cannot leak into the HOD view under any edge cases.

#### [MODIFY] [hod/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/BHU%20INTERNSHIP%20PROJECT/frontend/src/app/dashboard/hod/page.tsx)
- Add a strict role-guard `useEffect` to redirect any non-HOD user (e.g. Applicant) who accidentally navigates to the HOD page, which currently causes the HOD dashboard to render with an Applicant header.
- In the Application Review Modal, add a **"Download Document"** button alongside the "Approve" and "Reject" buttons.
- Wire the "Download Document" button to trigger the generation and download of a compiled PDF containing the applicant's details, photo, and signature.
- Remove any redundant UI elements inside the modal to strictly match "Approve, Reject, Download Document".

### Backend - Document Access

#### [MODIFY] [applications.controller.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/BHU%20INTERNSHIP%20PROJECT/backend/src/modules/applications/applications.controller.ts)
#### [MODIFY] [applications.service.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/BHU%20INTERNSHIP%20PROJECT/backend/src/modules/applications/applications.service.ts)
- Add or expose an endpoint (e.g., `GET /applications/:id/download`) for the HOD to securely download the applicant's document(s).

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Log in as an `HOD` and verify that the "New Application" button is completely absent from the top header and sidebar.
2. Attempt to manually navigate to `/dashboard/applicant/new` as an HOD and verify it redirects back.
3. Open an application in the HOD pending queue.
4. Verify the presence of the "Download Document" button.
5. Click "Download Document" and verify that the correct applicant documents are downloaded successfully.
6. Verify Approve and Reject functions still operate correctly.
